I am thinking...: Looking at line 1144-1145 in decoding.c:
```c
tlen = strlen(temp);
if (tlen > 0)
    _asn1_set_value(p, temp, tlen + 1);
```

This means if the OID decodes to an empty string (tlen == 0), the value is NOT set (remains NULL or whatever it was). Let me look at `asn1_get_object_id_der` to see when it might return an empty string.

Also, I notice that if `tlen == 0`, the node's value is not set, and it might remain uninitialized or NULL. But the check at line 849-853 in element.c would catch a NULL value by returning ASN1_VALUE_NOT_FOUND.

Actually wait - let me think about this differently. The uninitialized value might not be in libtasn1, but rather in how gnutls uses the data.

Let me look at the gnutls code more carefully.

